#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
dtUpdate — Common Desktop Environment (CDE) System & Application Update Manager

All-in-one updater for Debian packages (apt-get) and custom CDE desktop applications:
  1. Prompts securely for sudo password (validated via stdin pipe; never stored on disk)
  2. Runs `apt-get update` and inspects pending Debian package upgrades
  3. Analyzes installed CDE C/Motif binaries (`ldd`, `dpkg -S`, source timestamps) and
     Python/GTK/GStreamer CDE utilities to lay out a targeted CDE rebuild plan ONLY
     for apps affected by library updates, missing symbols, or newer local sources
  4. Presents the complete Debian + CDE Update Plan for explicit [Yes] / [No] confirmation
  5. On [Yes]: downloads packages with live progress bar, installs updates, recompiles
     needed CDE binaries atomically, restarts the CDE Workspace Manager (`dtwm`), and
     displays a comprehensive Overview Summary of everything changed.
"""

